#: src/moodlog:4622
msgid "Install Moodlog for Android: download Moodlog-Android-….apk from the latest release on GitHub (github.com/Akii-G/moodlog/releases) on your phone and open it. Android asks once to allow installing apps from your browser.\n\nIn the app, open Settings and enter the address and token above (pop-os.local works; if it doesn't, use the \"If that fails\" address). Tap Test connection. Your phone and this PC must be on the same Wi-Fi.\n\nFor sleep, steps and resting heart rate: in Settings → Health Connect, allow access, then turn on Send with each sync. Your watch or fitness app needs to share its data with Health Connect."
msgstr ""

#: src/moodlog:4629
msgid "Set this up once in the Shortcuts app on your iPhone. The iPhone and this PC must be on the same Wi-Fi, and this PC must be on when the shortcut runs.\n\nA. Build the shortcut\n1. Shortcuts → + → name it \"Moodlog Sync\".\n2. Add the action \"Find Health Samples\". Set Type to Steps. Add a filter: Start Date → is in the last → 7 days. Set Group By to Day.\n3. Add \"Repeat with Each\" (it repeats over the health samples). Inside it add a \"Text\" action with exactly:\n      steps;START;VALUE\n   Replace START and VALUE with the Repeat Item variable: insert it, tap it, and pick Start Date (set Date Format to ISO 8601) for the first and Value for the second.\n4. Below End Repeat add \"Add to Variable\" and name the variable Lines.\n5. Do steps 2–4 again with Type \"Resting Heart Rate\" and the text:\n      resting_hr;START;VALUE\n6. Do steps 2–4 again with Type \"Sleep\", Group By left off, and the text:\n      sleep;START;END;VALUE\n   (START = Start Date, END = End Date, both ISO 8601.)\n7. Add \"Combine Text\": combine Lines with New Lines.\n8. Add \"Get Contents of URL\". URL: the address above. Method: POST. Headers: add Authorization with the value \"Bearer \" followed by the token above. Request Body: JSON, with one Text field named data whose value is Combined Text.\n9. Add \"Show Result\", run the shortcut and allow Health access. It should answer \"OK. Stored …\". If lines were skipped, the answer says why.\n\nB. Run it every day\nAutomation tab → + → Time of Day → pick a time when you are normally using the phone (Health data cannot be read while the iPhone is locked) → Run Immediately → choose Moodlog Sync. Once it works, remove Show Result.\n\nEvery run sends the last 7 days, so days that were missed fill in on the next run.\nOther names you can send the same way: heart_rate, hrv, active_energy.\nIf the iPhone cannot connect and this PC has a firewall on, allow the port: sudo ufw allow 8765/tcp"
msgstr ""

